# Anti-spoof is protected

Face anti-spoof (liveness / PAD) is the main security and the purpose of the
timesheet attendance feature. A photo, video or phone screen must never be able
to mark attendance.

## Never without the user's explicit approval

- Change thresholds, tolerances or frame counts in
  `lib/core/site_management/face_recognition/antispoof/` (e.g.
  `antispoof_config.dart`, `burst_verification_pipeline.dart`,
  `on_device_pad_evaluator.dart`, `hybrid_liveness_gate.dart`).
- Skip, shorten, reorder or bypass the spoof check in
  `timesheet_capture_camera_panel.dart` (`_runCaptureTimePadBurst`,
  `_awaitFullPadBurst`, `_previewFaceIsLive`, the shutter single-frame check).
- Add "tolerate", "soft", "fallback", "fast path" or "fewer frames" logic to
  fix false rejections, crashes or speed. Propose it and wait for approval.

## Required behaviour (do not regress)

- Capture always runs the full burst (`AntispoofConfig.burstFrameCount`
  frames); never pass on 1–2 frames.
- Every capture attempt uses new frames taken after the press; never reuse
  frames from an earlier attempt or skip the check because one passed before.
- A frame is live only when print + replay < `maxLiveAttackSum` (0.10).
- `maxSoftSpoofFramesPerBurst` stays 0: any spoof frame blocks.
- A face wider than `maxFaceWidthFraction` (0.55) of the frame is refused
  ("Move back a little"), both on the live check and on every burst frame;
  a phone screen held so close that it fills the camera otherwise reads as live.
- Live stream frames given to the spoof models and matching are upright, so
  the ML Kit face box covers the face (`decodeCameraImageUpright`).
- Implement only the options the user approved, nothing extra.
- No employee name is shown on the camera for a face that fails the spoof check.
- Performance or crash fixes must keep the same spoof strength; if a trade-off
  is unavoidable, stop and explain it to the user first.
- After any change near this code, ask the user to test a photo, a video and
  another phone's screen on iPhone and Android before merging.
